The LEGB Rule in Python
This section explores how Python searches for variables and resolves names using the LEGB rule.
Concepts Covered
Local scope
Enclosing scope
Global scope
Built-in scope
Variable name resolution
Objective
Understand how Python determines which variable to use when the same name exists in different scopes.
Practice File
legb_rule.py
Key Takeaway
Python searches for names in this order: Local → Enclosing → Global → Built-in.
